.TH CTF-HUNTER-CAPTURE 8 "September 2026" "CTF Hunter 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ctf-hunter-capture \- provide capability-bound terminal capture for CTF Hunter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctf-hunter-capture preflight
.br
.B ctf-hunter-capture gate
.br
.B ctf-hunter-capture serve --socket
.I PATH
.RB [ --max-connections " N" ]
.br
.B ctf-hunter-capture run --uid
.I UID
.B --tty
.I PATH
.RB [ --tty " PATH ..." ]
.RB [ --duration-seconds " N" ]
.RB [ --show-payload ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctf-hunter-capture
is the privileged, capability-bound capture component. Production use is through
the system service and the
.B serve
command. The helper authenticates local clients and exposes only bounded events
accepted by the kernel privacy policy.
.PP
The diagnostic
.B run
mode is intended for controlled validation. Its
.B --show-payload
option prints accepted payload bytes and should not be enabled in routine service
operation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B preflight
Validate the running kernel's BTF layout and required terminal structures.
.TP
.B gate
Print the compiled privacy-gate controls.
.TP
.B serve
Serve authenticated daemon clients on a local Unix socket.
.TP
.B run
Run a time-bounded diagnostic capture for one UID and one or more terminals.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/ctf-hunter/capture.sock
Default production helper socket.
.TP
.I /sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux
Running-kernel BTF metadata.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctf-hunterd (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
